messages:
From: Karthik Iyer <karthik_iyer@redwood.com>
To: Marissa Cole <marissa_cole@redwood.com>, Mina Haddad <mina_haddad@redwood.com>
Date: 2027-04-22T11:03:00-07:00
Subject: Re: Request: 3yr price lock + uplift cap for multi-year commitment

Appreciate the fast turnaround. I reviewed Marissa's recommended controls and the workbook. Executive position: APPROVE the price lock and 8% uplift cap under these binding conditions:

- Commit: 36 months; minimum ARR commitment of $1.2M (annual) or equivalent prepaid credit;
- Uplift cap: 8% per year on published list for the agreed SKUs;
- Substitution: Redwood may substitute to functionally equivalent model variants if compute economics change, provided customer throughput/latency SLAs are met; any substitution will not exceed the 8% uplift cap in price impact over the prior year;
- Reporting & audit: quarterly usage / cost reports; right to audit if usage patterns deviate >25% from forecast;
- Early termination: customer may terminate after year 2 with 6 months' notice and an early termination fee equal to 20% of remaining committed value;

Condition: This approval is contingent on Finance confirming the ARR impact is within our exposure thresholds. Marissa, please engage Finance for the >$250k/year trigger and get CFO concurrence if it hits that mark.

I authorize Marissa to finalize the term sheet and issue a one-time exec exception for the attached deal. This approval expires in 7 days (2027-04-29) if we do not get signed commitment.

Karthik Iyer
VP, Sales — Redwood Inference
